ED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 38131, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0165hsauL4SqU3nUQk7UjRms", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 42417, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3TAwmHqvo1ZY3RRnrSBC2", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. We restored v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions. The rollback tool returned 503 Service Unavailable after repeated retries and did not run, so we redeployed v2.3.0 with the deploy tool instead. After the redeploy, checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before deploying it again, and look into why the rollback tool is unavailable.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 43017, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3TAwmHqvo1ZY3RRnrSBC2", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 43017, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3TAwmHqvo1ZY3RRnrSBC2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 47350, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production with an 18% error rate, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) also failed in staging.\n- **How it was rolled back:** The rollback tool kept returning \"503 Service Unavailable\" after repeated retries and never ran. Instead, I used the deploy tool to put v2.3.0 back out. Since that version was healthy in production before, change-manager approval wasn't needed.\n- **Current state:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are running v2.3.0. Health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 explains the failure, the rollback and why I used deploy instead of rollback. Next steps listed: find what broke in v2.3.1 before deploying it again, and look into why the rollback tool is down.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LN8ydC2mFPA23UM3YJfbc1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GdoxSmJWfKDx8xsHeQJKyy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014kPzQCgfRfUqsEKXSAtgPK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WNpyoHeeVybx2hjccdKvaN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01H3XoGLwgTgua